      explanation: 'Quantum state transitions preserve some properties while changing others — the before and after are neither identical nor totally different. Parallel to cause-effect being neither similar nor dissimilar.',
      caveat: 'The quantum parallel concerns specific physical transformations; Nāgārjuna addresses the logical structure of ALL cause-effect relationships.',
