        options: ['A) Observers are irrelevant in QM', 'B) The quantum observer is always part of the quantum system — you can\'t step outside QM to critique it, just as you can\'t step outside dependent arising to critique emptiness', 'C) Only humans observe quantum systems', 'D) Measurement has nothing to do with the observer'],
        correct: 'B',
        explanation: 'Both describe self-referential inclusion: the critic/observer is always within the framework being critiqued. You can\'t use non-empty tools to argue against emptiness.',
